Hi B12,
Bryan Balingit posted a new announcement in Ekonomiks 9-Einstein  
<https://classroom.google.com/c/MTkwMzY5NzI2MDA0>.

Good Afternoon, 9-Einstein!

For our 4rth Quarter, we will be trying a new approach in conducting our  
class and in tackling our lessons. Since the basic governing principle of  
our competencies is for you to meet a critical thinking standard, I decided  
to make use of this one effective strategy I always employ in achieving  
just that.

The Approach:

You guys are asked to read and comprehend our lessons found in this  
quarter's reference material which is already uploaded on your google  
classroom.

Every online synchronous sessions that we'll be having, I will be calling a  
number (6-8) of random names from the class that will be required to  
produce 3 Critical Questions about the lesson at hand. They will have these  
questions posted on the platform's chat/message box upon their names being  
called and will have it screen captured to serve as documentation once  
we're able to evaluate if the questions produced are indeed, critical or  
are constructed by way of critical thinking. This will be the sole output  
that I will be requiring you to submit this quarter.

What is a Critical Question?

There isn't a concise definition of what a critical question is. Critical  
Questioning on the other hand is, evaluating the validity/logic or  
basically, the truth in an argument or a claim. Answers to such questions  
cannot be quenched by way of memorizing the details and info that are found  
or are charitably provided by the reference material in use.



Further details about this new approach will be given during our  
synchronous class.


Topic to be read:

*KONSEPTO NG PAG-UNLAD w/ emphasis on *SAMA-SAMANG PAGKILOS PARA SA  
PAMBANSANG KAUNLARAN.
OPEN <https://classroom.google.com/c/MTkwMzY5NzI2MDA0/p/MzU3NjQ5MjQ0OTkz>
If you don't want to receive emails from Classroom, you can unsubscribe  
<https://classroom.google.com/s>.

